course: dictionary
lesson: 6492
title: Near: close in place, time and meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Near is a small word with many jobs. Most often it means close, not far away. «Bullies pick on children who are alone more often, so staying near friends and adults helps.» Near friends means close to friends, so you stay where they can reach you.
explain: Near can also be about time. «Summer is near» means summer is coming soon. Near can even mean almost, as in «a near miss», when something almost happens but does not. Check the clues around the word to choose the right meaning.
explain: Near works as more than one part of speech. As an adjective it describes things: the nearest shop is the closest one. As a verb, to near something means to come closer to it. Near by, or nearby, means close by, and nearly means almost.
fact: Near means close, not far away.
fact: «Nearest» means the closest one, so you can say the nearest shop or the nearest ten.
fact: «Near» can mean close in time, as in «Summer is near», or almost, as in «a near miss».
fact: To near something means to come closer to it.
fact: «Hammerhead sharks» gather in big schools «near islands», so near tells you where they are.
exercise: «Bullies pick on children who are alone more often, so staying near friends and adults helps.» What does staying near friends mean? | Making new friends | Staying far from friends | Forgetting all your friends | *Staying close to friends
exercise: «Summer is near.» What does near mean here? | Over and finished | Far away in distance | Painted green | *Close in time, coming soon
exercise: «Today giant mirrors and dishes see galaxies near the edge of the visible universe.» Which word in this sentence means close? | galaxies | *near | today | visible
test: In «a near miss», what does near mean? | Far away | *Almost, but it does not happen | Being cross with someone | Very close in distance
test: «Big ones work behind fences or slow down and stop near people.» Where do the big robots slow down and stop? | In the sea | *Near people | Far from fences | On the moon
exam: The bus stop is 10 metres away, the shop is 3 metres away and the park is 7 metres away. Which is the nearest? | Bus stop | *Shop | Park | Nobody, they are all the same
